<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!-- English strings for Glide.admx. -->
<policyDefinitionResources xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema"
                           xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
                           revision="1.0" schemaVersion="1.0"
                           xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/GroupPolicy/2006/07/PolicyDefinitions">
  <displayName>Glide</displayName>
  <description>Managed configuration for the Glide viewer and Windows host (Glide Cloud).</description>
  <resources>
    <stringTable>
      <string id="SUPPORTED_GlideManaged">Glide releases with managed mode (Glide Cloud)</string>
      <string id="Cat_Glide">Glide</string>
      <string id="Cat_Glide_Help">Connects the Glide viewer (glide-client.exe) and the Windows host (glide-host.exe) to your organization's Glide Cloud. Computer policies apply to everyone on the PC and take precedence over User policies.</string>

      <string id="CloudURL">Glide Cloud URL</string>
      <string id="CloudURL_Help">The address of your organization's Glide Cloud, for example https://glide.example.com (https only).

With this policy and an enrollment token, Glide enrolls the device in your organization when it starts, and sessions go through Glide Cloud: users sign in with your identity provider, and access follows your organization's policies.

The enrollment values (Glide Cloud URL, enrollment token, device name, tags) are read as one set: from the Computer policy if it sets a Glide Cloud URL, otherwise from the User policy.

Registry: SOFTWARE\Policies\Glide, CloudURL (REG_SZ).</string>

      <string id="EnrollmentToken">Enrollment token</string>
      <string id="EnrollmentToken_Help">The enrollment token from the Glide Cloud admin console (Enrollment tokens). Glide uses it once, to enroll the device; afterwards the device has its own credential, and you can revoke or rotate the token in the console without affecting enrolled devices.

Anyone who can read this machine's registry can read the token, so limit its use (expiry, maximum uses) in the console.

Registry: SOFTWARE\Policies\Glide, EnrollmentToken (REG_SZ).</string>

      <string id="DeviceName">Device name</string>
      <string id="DeviceName_Help">The name the device has in Glide Cloud, at most 64 characters. If not configured, the computer name is used.

Registry: SOFTWARE\Policies\Glide, DeviceName (REG_SZ).</string>

      <string id="Tags">Device tags</string>
      <string id="Tags_Help">Tags added to the device when it enrolls, one per line (for example: finance, floor-3). Access policies in Glide Cloud can match devices by tag. The enrollment token's default tags, if any, apply too.

Registry: SOFTWARE\Policies\Glide, Tags (REG_MULTI_SZ).</string>

      <string id="DisableLANMode">Turn off LAN mode</string>
      <string id="DisableLANMode_Help">If enabled, Glide does not listen for or make direct connections on the local network (TCP 7420 for the viewer, 7421 for the Windows host): only sessions through Glide Cloud are possible, with your organization's sign-in, policies and audit log.

This can only make Glide stricter than your organization's Glide Cloud setting: if either the Computer or the User policy enables it, LAN mode is off. If disabled or not configured, the Glide Cloud setting decides.

Registry: SOFTWARE\Policies\Glide, DisableLANMode (REG_DWORD, 1 = off).</string>
    </stringTable>
    <presentationTable>
      <presentation id="CloudURL">
        <textBox refId="CloudURL">
          <label>Glide Cloud URL:</label>
        </textBox>
      </presentation>
      <presentation id="EnrollmentToken">
        <textBox refId="EnrollmentToken">
          <label>Enrollment token:</label>
        </textBox>
      </presentation>
      <presentation id="DeviceName">
        <textBox refId="DeviceName">
          <label>Device name:</label>
        </textBox>
      </presentation>
      <presentation id="Tags">
        <multiTextBox refId="Tags">Tags (one per line):</multiTextBox>
      </presentation>
    </presentationTable>
  </resources>
</policyDefinitionResources>
